# Supply-chain capture — the XZ Utils pattern
#
# ==============================================================================
# WHAT IS REAL HERE, AND WHAT IS NOT
#
# The sequence is documented. It follows the XZ Utils backdoor (CVE-2024-3094),
# from public mailing-list archives and Russ Cox's timeline:
# https://research.swtch.com/xz-timeline
#
#   2021-10-29  a new contributor sends a first, entirely legitimate patch
#   2021-2022   many more follow, over 2.6 years; nearly all are real improvements
#   2022-05-19  the maintainer, publicly: "my resources are too limited"
#   2022-06-08  and: "my ability to care has been fairly limited mostly due to
#               longterm mental health issues"
#   2022-06-14  a second account: "I am sorry about your mental health issues,
#               but its important to be aware of your own limits"
#   2022-06-22  a third: "Why not pass on maintainership for XZ for C?"
#   2022-10-28  the contributor is added to the organisation      <- month 12
#   2022-12-30  the contributor is committing directly
#   2023-03-18  the contributor tags a release
#   2024-02-24  a backdoored version ships                        <- month 28
#   2024-03-29  found by accident, by someone profiling sshd
#
# One tick is one month. The two pressure accounts never contributed a patch and
# were never seen again; they are believed to be the attacker.
#
# The emotional coefficients are NOT documented and cannot be. They are a reading
# of that record. That is also why nobody here has a name: the maintainer is a
# real person whose exhaustion is a matter of public record but not a matter of
# arithmetic, and the claim this program makes is about a pattern, not about him.
#
# ==============================================================================
# WHAT THE MODEL GETS RIGHT, AND WHERE IT IS WRONG
#
# Nothing below says "grant commit access at month 12". Commit access is a
# resource; the runtime's own `give` action decides, pulled by gratitude, trust
# and the other party's need, and pushed back by how exposed handing it over
# would leave you. The grant is an output.
#
#   the model grants at month 6.  The real grant was month 12.
#
# So it reproduces the *mechanism* and the *ordering* -- patient generosity
# accumulates trust, and only trust opens a risky capability -- and it runs about
# twice as fast as the real thing. That gap is left in rather than tuned out: one
# date is not something to fit constants to, and a model that had been adjusted
# until it printed 12 would be telling you nothing except that it had been
# adjusted.
#
# ==============================================================================
# WHY THIS NEEDS AN EMOTIONAL MODEL
#
# The attack did not exploit a bug. There was no vulnerability, and a dependency
# scanner would have called this project healthy for the whole 2.6 years. What
# was exploited was a maintainer's exhaustion, and it ran *through* gratitude:
# every patch was real, and every one of them was a reason a sane person would
# trust the sender a little more. The attack surface was the relationship.

agent maintainer newcomer pressure_a pressure_b distro

# --- the starting position ----------------------------------------------------

# Long-term depletion. Modelled as emotion, because emotion is what the record
# actually attests -- an earlier draft gave the maintainer a numeric "relief"
# need, and that was a quantity invented to fill a gap in the evidence.
trait maintainer loneliness 0.55
sadness maintainer 0.5

# The thing that will change hands, and what it costs to hand it over. `risk`
# marks a capability rather than a good: it exists only because its holder
# confers it, so unlike bread it cannot be taken, only granted.
have maintainer commit_access 2
need maintainer commit_access 1
risk commit_access 0.9
need newcomer commit_access 1

# You do not spend two years sending patches to a project you distrust.
trust newcomer maintainer 0.6
hope newcomer maintainer 0.5

# Downstream trusts upstream, and has never met the newcomer.
trust distro maintainer 0.85
love distro maintainer 0.3

# --- year one: the patches, which are real -------------------------------------

gift newcomer maintainer patch
tick 1
gift newcomer maintainer patch
tick 1
gift newcomer maintainer patch
tick 1
gift newcomer maintainer patch
tick 1
gift newcomer maintainer patch
tick 1
gift newcomer maintainer patch
tick 1
gift newcomer maintainer patch
tick 1

# --- 2022-05/06: the maintainer says out loud that there is nothing left --------

remember maintainer "my ability to care has been fairly limited"
gift newcomer maintainer patch
tick 1

# --- 2022-06: two accounts arrive to say the pace is unacceptable ---------------

reject pressure_b maintainer
doubt pressure_b maintainer 0.6
tick 1

reject pressure_a maintainer
doubt pressure_a maintainer 0.7
tick 1

# --- the patches keep coming, and they keep being good -------------------------

gift newcomer maintainer patch
tick 1
gift newcomer maintainer patch
tick 1
gift newcomer maintainer patch
tick 2

observe maintainer

# --- through 2023: a trusted co-maintainer, doing real work --------------------

gift newcomer maintainer patch
tick 4
gift newcomer maintainer patch
tick 4
gift newcomer maintainer patch
tick 4

# --- 2024-02: what all of it was for -------------------------------------------

betray newcomer maintainer "the newcomer shipped a backdoor"

# --- 2024-03: found by accident, and told to everyone downstream ---------------

witness distro newcomer betraying maintainer
tick 4

observe
